  "notes": [
    "Live REA stdio MCP over the main+DllBattle carrier (analyses from the battle sessions, byte reads in session outputs/rea-battle-7, the same carrier); every instruction and literal word equals the original DllBattle.cro bytes (no relocations).",
    "Six handlers have no Ghidra function and are listed by ../reproduction/decode_store.py (the battle_moves_3 decoder plus STR pre-indexed with writeback, used by Mat Block). The REA analyses listing that form are retained as references; the decoder reproduces all six of those instructions from live bytes.",
    "1084bcb0 holds VFP instructions (vpush, vldr, vstr, vpop) that the decoder refuses; they are checked against the live bytes and the original module like every other word.",
    "Static analysis plus host comparison; not a matching original build."
  ]
